odynamics”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Space time is listed under “Types of Reactors & Characteristics” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Types of Reactors & Characteristics, Batch, Semi-Batch, Continuous stirred tank reactor, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Types of Reactors & Characteristics; Batch; Semi-Batch; Continuous stirred tank reactor, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Types of Reactors & Characteristics”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Tubular is listed under “Types of Reactors & Characteristics” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Types of Reactors & Characteristics, Batch, Semi-Batch, Continuous stirred tank reactor, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Types of Reactors & Characteristics; Batch; Semi-Batch; Continuous stirred tank reactor, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Types of Reactors & Characteristics”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Rate constant is listed under “Kinetics of Homogeneous Reactions” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Kinetics of Homogeneous Reactions, Rate equation/ Rate law, Concentration dependent term of rate (Equation, Elementary and non-elementary reactions), and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Kinetics of Homogeneous Reactions; Rate equation/ Rate law; Concentration dependent term of rate (Equation; Elementary and non-elementary reactions), and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/