VALUES (460009382507015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “NITROGENOUS FERTILIZERS”, how should production and storage be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS”, how should chemical properties and uses of Potassium Chloride be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS”, how should Potassium nitrate be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS”, how should Manufacturing of potassium chloride from sylvinite be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** production and storage is listed under “NITROGENOUS FERTILIZERS” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to NITROGENOUS FERTILIZERS, Ammonium Nitrate: Properties, Nitric acid: preparation and process flow diagram, Manufacturing of Nitric Acid by Pressure ammonia oxidation process and Intermediate pressure, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to NITROGENOUS FERTILIZERS; Ammonium Nitrate: Properties; Nitric acid: preparation and process flow diagram; Manufacturing of Nitric Acid by Pressure ammonia oxidation process and Intermediate pressure, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “NITROGENOUS FERTILIZERS”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** chemical properties and uses of Potassium Chloride is listed under “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS, Physical, Potassium nitrate, Potassium sulphate, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS; Physical; Potassium nitrate; Potassium sulphate, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Potassium nitrate is listed under “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS, Physical, chemical properties and uses of Potassium Chloride, Potassium sulphate, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS; Physical; chemical properties and uses of Potassium Chloride; Potassium sulphate, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Manufacturing of potassium chloride from sylvinite is listed under “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS, Physical, chemical properties and uses of Potassium Chloride, Potassium nitrate, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS; Physical; chemical properties and uses of Potassium Chloride; Potassium nitrate, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “POTASSIUM FERTILIZERS”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

