VALUES (460009382503015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Processing of Petroleum”, how should Visbreaking be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products”, how should Gasoline be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Processing of Petroleum”, how should Hydrocracking be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products”, how should Smoke Point be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Visbreaking is listed under “Processing of Petroleum” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Processing of Petroleum, Various types of cracking: Thermal cracking, catalytic cracking, Fluidised bed catalytic cracking and it’s dependency on temperature and pressure, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Processing of Petroleum; Various types of cracking: Thermal cracking; catalytic cracking; Fluidised bed catalytic cracking and it’s dependency on temperature and pressure, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Processing of Petroleum”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Gasoline is listed under “Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products, Primary treatment of crude : Dehydration and Desalting of crude oil, Various refinery products, Distillation of crude : Atmospheric Distillation, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products; Primary treatment of crude : Dehydration and Desalting of crude oil; Various refinery products; Distillation of crude : Atmospheric Distillation, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Cracking converts heavier hydrocarbons into smaller molecules; thermal or catalytic conditions influence products and selectivity.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Processing of Petroleum; Various types of cracking: Thermal cracking; catalytic cracking; Fluidised bed catalytic cracking and it’s dependency on temperature and pressure, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Processing of Petroleum”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Smoke Point is listed under “Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products, Primary treatment of crude : Dehydration and Desalting of crude oil, Various refinery products, Distillation of crude : Atmospheric Distillation, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products; Primary treatment of crude : Dehydration and Desalting of crude oil; Various refinery products; Distillation of crude : Atmospheric Distillation, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Properties of Crude and Petroleum Products”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

