INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (460009382506015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Properties of Polymers”, how should Electric Conductivity be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Plastics”, how should Polytetrafluoro Ethylene (PTFE /Teflon) be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Properties of Polymers”, how should Types: Bulk polymerization be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Plastics”, how should applications and manufacturing of: Polyethylene by high pressure ICI process for LDPE be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Electric Conductivity is listed under “Properties of Polymers” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Properties of Polymers, Polymerization, Types: Bulk polymerization, Solution polymerization. Suspension polymerization, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Properties of Polymers; Polymerization; Types: Bulk polymerization; Solution polymerization. Suspension polymerization, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Properties of Polymers”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Polytetrafluoro Ethylene (PTFE /Teflon) is listed under “Plastics” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Plastics, Properties, applications and manufacturing of: Polyethylene by high pressure ICI process for LDPE, Polyethylene by Ziegler low pressure process for HDPE, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Plastics; Properties; applications and manufacturing of: Polyethylene by high pressure ICI process for LDPE; Polyethylene by Ziegler low pressure process for HDPE, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Plastics”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Polymerization joins monomer units to form polymers; reaction mechanism and conditions determine molecular weight and polymer structure.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Properties of Polymers; Polymerization; Solution polymerization. Suspension polymerization; Emulsion polymerization. Molecular weight, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Properties of Polymers”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** applications and manufacturing of: Polyethylene by high pressure ICI process for LDPE is listed under “Plastics” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Plastics, Properties, Polyethylene by Ziegler low pressure process for HDPE, Polypropylene, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Plastics; Properties; Polyethylene by Ziegler low pressure process for HDPE; Polypropylene, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Plastics”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

