VALUES (4600093825060129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain and apply Polymerization in “Properties of Polymers”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Classification of Rubber and its Properties in “Rubbers”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Properties in “Plastics”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply applications and manufacturing of: Viscose rayon fibres in “Fibres”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Polymerization converts monomers into polymers; conditions affect molecular weight, structure and properties.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Types: Bulk polymerization, Solution polymerization. Suspension polymerization, Emulsion polymerization. Molecular weight, Crystallinity and Glass transition temperature. Properties of Plastics: Electrical Resistance.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Classification of Rubber and its Properties is covered in “Rubbers”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Various types of rubber, Applications and Manufacturing of: Ethylene Propylene Terpolymers Butyl rubber Polyurethane, Silicone rubber, Rubbers, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Various types of rubber, Applications and Manufacturing of: Ethylene Propylene Terpolymers Butyl rubber Polyurethane, Silicone rubber, Rubbers.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Properties is covered in “Plastics”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to applications and manufacturing of: Polyethylene by high pressure ICI process for LDPE, Polyethylene by Ziegler low pressure process for HDPE, Polypropylene, Polystyrene, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to applications and manufacturing of: Polyethylene by high pressure ICI process for LDPE, Polyethylene by Ziegler low pressure process for HDPE, Polypropylene, Polystyrene.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** applications and manufacturing of: Viscose rayon fibres is covered in “Fibres”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Cellulose Acetate fibre, Nylon-6, Glass fibres, Fibres, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Cellulose Acetate fibre, Nylon-6, Glass fibres, Fibres.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

