VALUES (460009382501015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Crystallization”, how should construction and working of Swenson Walker be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Crystallization”, how should classification of crystallizer be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Humidification”, how should Dew Point be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Adsorption”, how should various equipments for adsorption be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Crystallization forms crystals from a supersaturated solution or melt; temperature, concentration and nucleation influence crystal size and purity.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Crystallization; Concept and application; methods for super saturation; classification of crystallizer, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Crystallization”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Crystallization forms crystals from a supersaturated solution or melt; temperature, concentration and nucleation influence crystal size and purity.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Crystallization; Concept and application; methods for super saturation; Meir’s theory, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Crystallization”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Dew Point is listed under “Humidification” in the syllabus. Define it, explain the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or governing conditions, relate it to Humidification, Importance of Humidification operation in Chemical Industry, Definitions: Absolute Humidity, Relative Humidity, and show how it is applied to a chemical-engineering operation. State important assumptions and a way to verify the outcome.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Humidification; Importance of Humidification operation in Chemical Industry; Definitions: Absolute Humidity; Relative Humidity, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Humidification”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Adsorption accumulates molecules at a surface, unlike absorption into the bulk of a phase; capacity and equilibrium are important.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, relate it to Adsorption; Definition and Industrial application; Types of Adsorption; commonly used Adsorbents in Chemical Industries, and state the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. Define assumptions and keep units consistent.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a chemical-engineering process, material, product or equipment task in “Adsorption”. State the expected result and the reason for the selected approach.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the outcome with the stated objective, and mention a relevant source of error, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

